cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Biology as Code: an open, provenance-tracked toolkit for meal digestion and metabolic-pathway modeling (reference implementation of FDP-1)"
abstract: >-
  biology-as-code is an open-source toolkit that models what happens to a meal —
  digestion, absorption, and the metabolic pathways it drives — as inspectable code:
  a meal-simulation pipeline, a declarative model of the GI tract as versioned state
  machines, teaching metabolic-pathway graphs, LAW-SPEC law cards as queryable data, and
  an evidence/provenance layer. It is a reference implementation of FDP-1, the Food Data
  Provenance Declaration — a minimal specification for declaring the provenance of a
  nutrient value and the validation status of any score computed from it — which is
  published separately as its own citable standard at github.com/murffious/fdp-1. This
  record covers the Python package. It does NOT claim authorship of the data in
  MASTER_CROSSWALK.tsv: eight of that table's twelve columns derive from a Virtual
  Metabolic Human / Recon3D export and must be cited to VMH (doi:10.1093/nar/gky992,
  doi:10.1038/nbt.4072). See NOTICE and THIRD-PARTY-DATA.json.
  Built to be fail-closed with no fabricated data. Teaching / research software;
  not medical advice.
